benchmem - memory allocator benchmarks for thesis comparison

Description:
The 'benchmem' command runs malloc-focused benchmark scenarios and prints
machine-readable metrics for comparing segmentation and paging branches.

Scenarios:
  expand - Sequential malloc without free (cold heap growth / MM expansion)
  churn  - Repeated malloc and free of the same size
  frag   - Allocate blocks, free every other, re-allocate (fragmentation)
  peak   - Grow heap in fixed-size blocks until allocation fails
  all    - Run all scenarios sequentially

Each scenario reports:
  elapsed_cycles - CPU cycles via RDTSC (primary timing metric)
  elapsed_ms     - wall time via SYS_UPTIME (may be 0 for short runs; PIT ~1 ms)
  iterations, failures, user/kernel heap addresses, arena/used/free bytes,
  payload size, and allocator overhead.

Usage:
benchmem <scenario> [args...]
benchmem help

Examples:
benchmem expand
benchmem expand 150 4096
benchmem churn 500 256
benchmem frag 200 128
benchmem peak 4096
benchmem all
